  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Present workflows",
      "items": [
        "Ticket files land via factory-write-tickets. factory-promote opens GitHub issues from docs/tickets.",
        "Dispatcher is factory-dispatch (gh-aw lock + markdown, Copilot). agent-router and dispatch-router route by usage limits and agent preference (claude, codex, cursor); Freebuff and OpenCode are manual fallbacks. It routes; it does not implement the ticket.",
        "Lanes: factory-lane-claude, factory-lane-cursor, factory-lane-codex. Checks present: CI, scope-guard, config-guard, Security.",
        "factory-quiet-hours gates new work 22:00-09:00 Asia/Jerusalem."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Review and ship",
      "items": [
        "Batch loop (factory-batch, factory/LOOP.md): component PRs merge into batch/<loop-id>; ONE Cursor Bugbot review runs on the batch PR. factory-review-fix sends findings back to the lane, max 3 rounds, then blocked:amit.",
        "Ship: batch PR enters the GitHub merge queue (enqueue via GraphQL) into integration, then Vercel preview plus convex-deploy-test to ceaseless-dog-617. Queue enabled on the repo: UNKNOWN.",
        "Live: Amit runs Release to production (release.yml). It opens one integration to master release PR, re-runs CI, secret scans, Playwright and Bugbot, deploys Convex prod only if convex/ changed, merges, then checks www.tempoflow.dev/api/health. Rollback is manual. deploy-live.yml also exists."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Pause and failure",
      "items": [
        "FACTORY_PAUSED_ALL or FACTORY_PAUSED skips factory jobs. force=true on workflow_dispatch runs anyway, and the lane and dispatcher steps reject a bot actor.",
        "factory-failures.yml describes the failure branch: after 3 failed fixes, blocked:amit.",
        "config-guard.yml is present (same check family as scope-guard). It is named in the Checks card because a node has only three source slots."
      ]
    }
  ]
